<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcmaeonidae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alcmaeonids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alcmaeonids were a powerful noble family of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. They were accused of sacrilege for killing followers of Cylon in a sanctuary around 632 BCE, and spent periods in exile. During one such exile, after a fire in 548 BCE, they rebuilt the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> at Delphi with a marble façade, winning the oracle's favour. Their members included the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleisthenes">Cleisthenes</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> was an Alcmaeonid through his mother.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcmaeonidae.jpg" alt="Alcmaeonidae" width="320" height="534" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographerUnknown photographer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greece_from_the_Coming_of_the_Hellenes_to_AD._14,_page_137,_Pericles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
